kel.desc:
commented npm modules not ignored if comments are multi-line
Given this code in an editor pane:

```js
    // const cow = require('cow');
    /* const say = require('say'); */
    /**
     * const hello = require('hello'); 
     * const world = require('world'); 
    */
```

Fiddle will still attempt to install the `say`, `hello`, and `world` packages from NPM. This is because we only check if lines start with `//` to check if they're commented.
