issue:
statement local is not limiting scope of variables
Executing the following example script with zeek 7.0.5
```
module Test;
export {
    function func1(){
        local t: string = "test";
        print t;
    }
    function func2(){
        local t: string = "test";
        print t;
    }
}

event zeek_init() {
    func1();
    func2();
}
```
leads to the errors
```
error in ./test.zeek, line 4: already a global identifier (Test::t)
error in ./test.zeek, line 4 and ./test.zeek, line 8: already defined (Test::t)
```

Removing the export block runs as expected without errors. Is this intended behavior? The zeek documentation doesn't mention anything for [local](https://docs.zeek.org/en/master/script-reference/statements.html#keyword-local) and [export](https://docs.zeek.org/en/master/script-reference/statements.html#keyword-export)

